      "AgentStructuredContent (semantic 35, components/prism-next/agent-structured-content.tsx) declares Inline + dedicated workspace content. 35 edits content hierarchies; 28 AgentDocumentWorkspace reads manuscripts and edits chapter bodies; 12 arranges paper/task items and their order. Directory selection is not content editing. Reuse Tree/TreeItem/TreeItemLabel with existing headless-tree sync loader, keyboard navigation and drag-and-drop, plus Card, fixed-label Input, Prism Button navigation, Badge and RecordDetails/Collapsible. Tree has no editing data model: compose separate node tools without modifying Tree/coss or adding a catalog entry, dependency, visual token, store, persistence, execution or Workspace types. Nodes and parent/child relationships stay structured; this is a host projection, not a universal AST.",
      "Structure props require structure={id,title,version:{id,label},baseVersion?,snapshot?,currentVersion?}, nodes:readonly {id,title,type,level,status,summary?,children?,capabilities?}[] and selectedNodeId:string|null. IDs remain callback/key references; display names and version labels only. Root level is 1; empty/duplicate IDs, cycles or inconsistent levels stop tree/actions. Status is normal|added|modified|deleted (deleted means pending submission), or conflict|readonly with mandatory reason. Global capabilities require view/rename/add/delete/move/nest, each supported(reason?) or limited|unsupported(reason required). Node overrides only narrow capabilities. Host supplies permitted content, version, history and save facts; component does not infer permission.",
      "onSelect emits {structureId,versionId,nodeId}; selection changes only via props. expandedIds/onExpandedChange optionally control view-only folding; otherwise local expansion defaults to roots, with no business selection state. Clicking titles or Enter/Space requests selection; arrows and folder buttons expand/collapse separately. Native navigation-size up/down/outdent/indent buttons are touch and keyboard equivalents of drag and remain visible when their capability exists. Same-parent moves use move; reparenting uses nest. Drag rejects external data, does not auto-expand on a timer, and shares all move guards with buttons. Read-only/conflict/deleted nodes and ancestors cannot be edited; affected descendants are checked for whole-subtree moves/deletion; cycles, no-op, missing/restricted parents and invalid indexes are rejected.",
