      "view=inline|workspace defaults inline and density=default|compact defaults default. Inline shows the first two levels, all supplied node count/depth and host changes={baseVersion:{id,label},summary:string[]}; missing summary stays unconfirmed, [] records no changes. Workspace provides full collapsible Tree, host changes, selected-node summary and editing tools. Compact only tightens spacing, preserving deep conflicts, readonly/pending-deletion and node restrictions outside collapsed tree/details. snapshot presence including empty string marks historical readonly; currentVersion label is separate. save={state:unsaved|saved-draft|submitted|conflict|unknown,description?} defaults unknown and never changes on click. onExpand exposes 编辑结构 or 查看完整结构 only when supplied and viewable; onBack requests host return, never saving or discarding. notice is at most one boundary hint; details is supplementary collapsed text, with duplicate capability reasons grouped.",
      "#structured-content has labelled lesson-outline and textbook examples, each inline/workspace/compact and a 320px toggle. Lesson includes five stages, child activities, added nodes and movement; its adapter only updates page memory and explicitly unsaved example facts. Textbook is limited viewing, with edits/movement unsupported and explained. Historical and deep-conflict samples do not rewrite the current draft. SSR/handler/type tests cover intents and boundaries; browser themes, actual drag/touch/focus, Workspace integration, screen reader and services remain unverified. Read-only Workspace main review is a proposed same-object 正文/结构 view using session-owned hierarchy, not an implemented integration.",

      "AgentArtifactOutput (semantic 33, components/prism-next/agent-artifact-output.tsx) declares Inline + dedicated workspace content. 27 AgentExecutionResult reports execution facts; 33 handles format, layout, range, version and file delivery, and they may compose without overriding unknown-receipt restrictions. 28 AgentDocumentWorkspace reads/edits manuscripts and may open 33 through its declared export capability. QuestionPrint is an optional preview slot with unchanged browser pagination/printing; printing or content preview does not establish a downloadable service file. Reuse Card, Field, Select, Prism Badge/Button and RecordDetails; no catalog entry, dependency, visual token, generator, runtime, store, persistence or Workspace private types.",
      "Artifact output requires artifact={id,title,version:{id,label}}, formats:{id,label,support:supported|lossy|unsupported}[], layouts/ranges/versions:{id,label,disabledReason?}[], controlled value={formatId,layoutId,rangeId,versionId} (each string|null), and output:AgentArtifactOutputRecord. Lossy requires risk and unsupported requires reason; both remain visible and unsupported cannot generate. recommendedFormatId is optional; inline generates with only that recommendation plus the supplied layout/range/version, without changing value.formatId. Workspace uses the selected format and four fixed-label Selects. Missing/invalid selection is never replaced with the first item. Internal references remain in events/keys only; primitive option values are local indices, not opaque IDs.",
      "AgentArtifactOutputRecord={id,artifactId,title,version:{id,label},format,layout,range,status} holds the then-configuration independently of current selectors. status is idle(description?), generating(request:{id,runId},progress?,description?), ready(file,description?), failed(reason), unknown(request,reason,query?), expired(reason) or forbidden(reason). Only explicit finite 0..100 generating progress is shown; no progress means no percentage, and 100 never becomes ready. Any current output/queue unknown makes the card query-only: no edits, generation, download, expansion or preview. onQuery({artifactId,recordId,versionId,request}) addresses each exact original request/run. Missing query capability or association explains unavailability; no replacement generation. Generating freezes edits/generation. Idle/ready/failed may request generation with explicit capability; expired/forbidden cannot.",
      "File={id,name,version:{id,label},sizeBytes?,generatedAt?,download?:{label,disabledReason?}}. A download entry requires ready, valid matching record/file version, same artifact, file.download and onDownload. It emits only {artifactId,recordId,versionId,fileId}; no href/raw storage path or generated URL is accepted. Host must attest an actual currently accessible file and recheck current permission on delivery. Missing time/size stays unconfirmed; path-like names are not displayed. A file matching its own record but differing from current artifact version is visibly 基于旧版本 and retains its exact version. Expired/forbidden ignore untyped file payloads. Permission/disclosure of all labels/content/slots remains a trusted host duty, never inferred by UI.",
      "onValueChange and onGenerate emit {artifactId,currentVersionId,options} with copied selection fields; no callback return creates file/state facts. Missing onValueChange is readonly; missing onGenerate hides generation. generateDisabledReason presence, invalid selection and identity/duplicate-ID checks guard handlers as well as presentation. queue contains same-artifact records in supplied order, with no built-in batch executor. history is passive then-snapshots with no query/download/generate; historical file access requires separately supplied current authorization/availability. Omitted records do not assert absence, explicit [] shows no records. All records remain visible in both views/densities, including failures and old versions.",
      "Artifact output view=inline|workspace defaults inline; density=default|compact defaults default and is not a third state. Workspace mounts only host-supplied preview for selected range/version; unknown, invalid association and expired/forbidden suppress it. Optional onExpand(trigger) exposes 更多输出选项 in inline only; onBack is host navigation. notice is at most one persistent boundary hint and details is passive collapsed supplementary copy. Critical risks, unsupported/failed/unknown/old-version and disabled reasons never move into details or disappear in compact. #artifact-output offers paper PDF/Word-lossy/QuestionPrint/v1 history and report PDF-generating-without-progress/Excel-unsupported/unknown-queue examples, all three uses and 320px. Export/download/query actions only show labelled example feedback; independently loaded samples are not execution receipts. Browser, actual printing/delivery, Workspace and real-service verification remain separate.",

